@NODE iNTRODUCTiON "iNTRODUCTiON OF SYSA VERSiON 1.1"

SYSOP-ALARMiNATOR VERSiON 1.1 iS A TOOL WHO iNFORMS THE SYSOP ABOUT
CERTAiN USERS WHEN THEY ARE LOGGiNG iNTO THE BBS.
iT HAS @{"FEATURES" LiNK FEATURES} THAT OTHER TOOLS DOESN'T HAVE.

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF SYSA VERSiON 1.1"

i DECiDED TO CODE THiS TOOL BECAUSE i LiKED THE USER-ALARMiNATOR V1.0
RELEASED BY ABSTURZ-DESiGN LONG TiME AGO. THE USER-ALARMiNATOR V1.0
FROM ABSTURZ-DESiGN iS VERY NiCE, BUT iT HAS SOME FEATURES MiSSiNG.
iT ONLY LOOKS iNTO A CONFiG-FiLE FOR THE USER-NAMES AND THEN WHEN iT
FiNDS THE USER WHiCH iS LOGGiNG iNTO YOUR BBS SiMPLY PLAYS A SAMPLE
TO iNFORM THE SYSOP.

iT HAS NO CONFiG-FiLES AND WORKS FULLY WiTH TOOL-TYPES iN THE iCON.

MY VERSiON HAS LOTSA MORE OPTiONS. iT LOOKS FOR THE FOLLOWiNG THiNGS:

 1. USER-NAME
 2. ACCESS-AREA
 3. ACCESS-LEVEL

    OR ANY COMBiNATiON OF THOSE...


iF YOU WANT TO SEND A PERSONAL MESSAGE ALSO TO THE USER EVEN WHEN YOU
DON'T WANT TO ALERTED WHEN HE iS LOGGiNG ON... NO PROBLEM!

SYSOP-ALARMiNATOR V1.1 LOOKS WHENEVER THE TOOL iS STARTED FOR A SPECiAL
TEXTFiLE WHiCH iS ONLY FOR THE USER WHO iS LOGGiNG ON.

LOOK iNTO @{"PRiVATE SCREEN" LiNK SCREENS} FOR MORE iNFORMATiON.

AND NOW i THiNK i GAVE YOU ENOUGH REASONS TO iNSTALL SYSA V1.1 :)

@ENDNODE

@NODE iNSTALLATiON "iNSTALLATiON OF SYSA VERSiON 1.1"

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V2.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV2.xx}.

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V3.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV3.xx}.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMiEXPRESSV2.xx "iNSTALLATiON TO AMi EXPRESS V2.xx"

TO iNSTALL THE DOOR LOAD UP THE CUSTOMCOMMANDS (/X V2.2x OR BELOW) OR
SYS.CMD (/X V2.3x) AND ADD THE FOLLOWiNG LiNE TO THE LiST.


          11 SPACES iN         
          |
-------------------------------------------          
*ALARM    RM010MODULES:MM_TOOLS/ALARM/ALARM
-------------------------------------------
||        |||  |           
||        |||  ` 'MODULES:MM_TOOLS/ALARM/ALARM' iS THE LOCATiON OF
||        |||     THE FiLE.
||        |||
||        ||` 001 THE MiNiMUM ACCESS TO USE THiS DOOR. CHANGE iT TO WHAT
||        ||      YOU LiKE.
||        ||
||        |` 'M' FOR A MULTiNODE BBS ('S' FOR A SiNGLE NODE BBS).
||        |
||        ` 'R' FOR A REXX DOOR WHiCH WiLL USE THE 'REXXDOOR'-UTiL.
||
|`COMMAND TO START THE DOOR.
|
`-RETARD OPTiON. TO MAKE SURE THEY ONLY USE 'ALARM' & ONLY  'ALARM'
  TO GET THE DOOR TO COME UP. iF NOT USED, THiNGS SUCH AS 'ALARMO'
  AND 'ALARMATRON' WOULD STiLL BRiNG UP THE DOOR.


  USE THE LiNE BETWEEN THE LiNES ONLY. THE OTHER PARTS ARE JUST AN
  EXPLANATiON TO MAKE SURE YOU KNOW WHAT EACH PART iS DOiNG (SiNCE
  NOONE WOULD TELL ME BACK iN THE DAYS WHERE i DiDN'T KNOW WHAT WAS
  GOiNG ON!)  

  NOW COPY THE DiRECTORY 'MODULES' FROM THE LHA-ARCHiEV TO YOUR BBS.

  AT LAST EDiT THE @{"TOOLTYPES" LiNK TOOLTYPES} OF 'ALARM.iNFO'. YOU
  WiLL FiND iT iN 'BBS:MODULES/MM_TOOLS/ALARM/'.


  NOW ADD THE FOLLOWiNG TO YOUR LOGON.TXT AND LOGON.TXT.GR

  --------------CUT HERE----------------
  ~CC_ALARM
  --------------CUT HERE----------------

 
  THAT'S ALL...

@ENDNODE

