@ENDNODE

@NODE TOOLTYPES "HOW TO EDiT THE TOOLTYPES?"

  ACSTYPE=<number>                       THE <number> DEFiNES FOR WHAT THE
                                         SYSOP WANTS TO BE ALERTED.
                                         1 = NAMES ONLY
                                         2 = ACCESS-AREA ONLY
                                         3 = ACCESS-LEVEL ONLY
                                         4 = NAMES & ACCESS-AREA
                                         5 = NAMES & ACCESS-LEVEL
                                         6 = ACCESS-AREA & ACCESS-LEVEL
                                         7 = NAMES & ACCESS-AREA &
                                             ACCESS-LEVEL

                                         E.G.: ACSTYPE=1 <- iS LOOKiNG
                                                            FOR USER-NAME
                                                            ONLY !!!


  ACSLEVEL=<number>                      THE <number> DEFiNES THE 
                                         ACCESS-LEVEL OF THE USER BY WHiCH
                                         THE SYSOP WANTS TO BE ALERTED WHEN
                                         THiS OPTiON iS CHOSEN.

                                         E.G.: ACSLEVEL=200


  ACSAREA=<area>                         THE <area> DEFiNES THE ACCESS-AREA
                                         OF THE USER BY WHiCH THE SYSOP
                                         WANTS TO BE ALERTED WHEN THiS
                                         OPTiON iS CHOSEN.

                                         E.G.: ACSAREA=OSiRiS


  USER.01=<user>                          THE <user> DEFiNES THE USER-NAME BY
                                         WHiCH THE SYSOP WANTS TO BE ALERTED
                                         WHEN THiS OPTiON iS CHOSEN.

                                         E.G.: USER.01=MUMU
                                               USER.02=SPiDER
                                               USER.03=HELiON

                                         !!! YOU CAN ADD AS MANY USERS AS
                                             YOU WANT !!!


  SAMPLECONFiG=<path&options>            THE <path&options> DEFiNES THE PATH
                                         OF THE SAMPLE-PLAYER AND THE SAMPLE
                                         WiTH iTS OPTiONS WHiCH WiLL BE
                                         PLAYED WHEN THE SYSOP iS ALERTED.

  E.G.:

  SAMPLECONFiG=SYS:C/RAWPLAY 430 63 BBS:MODULES/MM_TOOLS/ALARM/ALARM.SAMPLE

  THAT SHOULD BE ALL FOR NOW...


@ENDNODE       

@NODE SCREENS "HOW TO BUiLT iN THE PRiVATE SCREENS?"

iF YOU WANT TO SEND A PERSONAL MESSAGE TO A USER EVEN WHEN YOU
DON'T WANT TO ALERTED WHEN HE iS LOGGiNG ON... NO PROBLEM!

SYSOP-ALARMiNATOR V1.1 LOOKS WHENEVER THE TOOL iS STARTED FOR A SPECiAL
TEXTFiLE WHiCH iS ONLY FOR THE USER WHO iS LOGGiNG ON.

MAKE A TEXTFiLE THAT SHOULD BE SHOWN TO THE SPECiAL USER AND NAME HiM
'ALARM.USER.<number>'. THE <number> iS THE SLOTNUMBER OF THE USER WHO
SHOULD GET THE TEXTFiLE.

EXAMPLE: 'ALARM.USER.3'    <--- NOW THE USER WiTH THE SLOTNUMBER 3
                                WiLL GET THE TEXTFiLE.

 !!! ATTENTiON !!!

MAYBE YOU JUST WANT TO ANNOY A USER WiTH A PERSONAL TEXTFiLE BEFORE
DELETiNG HiM. AFTER YOU DELETED THE USER iT MAY BE HAPPEN THAT ANOTHER
USER HAS NOW THE SAME SLOTNUMBER WHiCH THE DELETED USER HAD. NOW THE NEW
USER WiLL GET THE PRiVATE TEXTFiLE. TAKE CARE OF THE PRiVATE TEXTFiLES
SO NOBODY WiLL GET A TEXTFiLE WHO SHOULD NEVER GET ONE.

NOW COPY THE 'ALARM.USER.<number>' iNTO 'BBS:MODULES/MM_TOOLS/ALARM/'.

THAT SHOULD BE ALL...

@ENDNODE

